WEBVTT

1
00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:09.638
CBR900RR

2
00:04:45.345 --> 00:04:48.480
When you're underwater
for months at a time,

3
00:04:48.482 --> 00:04:50.749
you lose all sense
of day and night.

4
00:04:52.052 --> 00:04:55.188
And there's only awake
and dreaming.

5
00:04:56.957 --> 00:04:58.992
Not that those things
are easy to tell apart.

6
00:05:04.498 --> 00:05:05.964
I think,

7
00:05:05.966 --> 00:05:07.932
or I dream about
the first thing

8
00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.202
he ever said to me.

9
00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:17.110
Told me he didn't
believe in time...

10
00:05:18.612 --> 00:05:19.778
only moments.

11
00:05:21.281 --> 00:05:23.014
Hmm.

12
00:05:23.016 --> 00:05:24.417
He was a
glass-half-full type.

13
00:05:25.452 --> 00:05:26.652
All right.

14
00:05:29.055 --> 00:05:30.290
I prefer it empty.

15
00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.764
What are you doing here?

16
00:05:43.236 --> 00:05:45.738
I mean, there's a
comfort to cynicism.

17
00:05:48.774 --> 00:05:50.143
There's a lot
less to lose.

18
00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:09.520
Wake up!

19
00:07:09.522 --> 00:07:11.157
Pressure breach!

20
00:07:15.262 --> 00:07:16.793
Pressure breach!
We gotta get to the bulkhead!

21
00:07:16.795 --> 00:07:18.263
Structural
integrity compromised.

22
00:07:18.265 --> 00:07:20.133
Everyone up! Everyone up!
Come on!

23
00:07:24.271 --> 00:07:26.973
Structural integrity
compromised.

24
00:07:28.041 --> 00:07:29.741
What the hell is happening?

25
00:07:29.743 --> 00:07:31.044
Let's go! Pressure breach!

26
00:07:34.014 --> 00:07:35.413
We gotta seal the bulkhead!

27
00:07:35.415 --> 00:07:37.781
De-pressurization
warning.

28
00:07:37.783 --> 00:07:40.251
Seal the bulkhead.

29
00:07:40.253 --> 00:07:42.687
- De-pressurization warning.
- I don't have my keycard!

30
00:07:42.689 --> 00:07:43.923
Here, here, here.

31
00:07:45.425 --> 00:07:46.457
- No!
- Bulkhead jammed.

32
00:07:46.459 --> 00:07:48.693
I gotta get inside
this thing now!

33
00:07:48.695 --> 00:07:50.230
- Reboot required.
- Where is it? Where is it?

34
00:07:52.766 --> 00:07:53.765
Oh, my God!

35
00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:55.466
Come on!

36
00:07:55.468 --> 00:07:59.105
De-pressurization warning.
Seal the bulkhead.

37
00:08:00.473 --> 00:08:01.973
Come on, come on,
come on, come on.

38
00:08:01.975 --> 00:08:03.241
The whole rig
is about to implode!

39
00:08:03.243 --> 00:08:04.475
If you don't shut these doors,

40
00:08:04.477 --> 00:08:05.977
it'll take the whole station
with us!

41
00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:08.012
Okay! Okay, okay, okay,
got it, got it, got it!

42
00:08:08.014 --> 00:08:09.380
- System online.
- Shut the door!

43
00:08:09.382 --> 00:08:11.549
- Wait!
- Hey, hey, hey.

44
00:08:11.551 --> 00:08:12.550
Wait for us!

45
00:08:12.552 --> 00:08:13.384
- Hey!
- Run!

46
00:08:13.386 --> 00:08:14.919
- Run!
- Come on!

47
00:08:14.921 --> 00:08:16.621
Guys, run! Come on, come on!

48
00:08:16.623 --> 00:08:18.489
- Hey! Hey, hey!
- Come on, guys, let's go!

49
00:08:18.491 --> 00:08:19.957
Come on, run!

50
00:08:19.959 --> 00:08:22.026
Norah, Norah!
They're not gonna make it.

51
00:08:22.028 --> 00:08:23.795
- Close the door!
- Norah!

52
00:08:23.797 --> 00:08:25.999
We have to close the door,
otherwise the whole rig will die.

53
00:08:29.169 --> 00:08:30.203
Shut the door now!

54
00:09:18.785 --> 00:09:20.918
Structural failure is imminent

55
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.153
as the result of an...

56
00:09:22.155 --> 00:09:23.590
incident.

57
00:09:26.259 --> 00:09:30.728
To all Kepler Station crew,
structural failure is imminent.

58
00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:34.567
Repeat, structural
failure is imminent.

59
00:09:36.336 --> 00:09:38.703
Hey, hey.

60
00:09:38.705 --> 00:09:39.606
You okay?

61
00:09:42.909 --> 00:09:44.344
Was that an earthquake?

62
00:09:45.545 --> 00:09:46.413
I don't know.

63
00:09:49.215 --> 00:09:51.151
Had to have been like
a ten or eleven.

64
00:09:52.285 --> 00:09:54.452
I don't even know
what channel we'd be...

65
00:09:54.454 --> 00:09:57.021
All personnel
report to pod bays

66
00:09:57.023 --> 00:09:58.891
for immediate evacuation.

67
00:10:00.226 --> 00:10:02.160
This is Kepler.
Control, can you hear me?

68
00:10:02.162 --> 00:10:06.531
Kepler Station
status, 70% compromised.

69
00:10:06.533 --> 00:10:08.166
Reactor unstable.

70
00:10:08.168 --> 00:10:09.567
Control, this is Kepler,
can you hear me?

71
00:10:09.569 --> 00:10:12.838
Kepler Station
status, 70% compromised.

72
00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.006
Mayday. Mayday. Mayday.

73
00:10:15.008 --> 00:10:16.607
Can anyone hear me?

74
00:10:27.754 --> 00:10:28.655
We have to get to the pod bays.

75
00:10:29.924 --> 00:10:30.990
Come on.

76
00:10:37.664 --> 00:10:40.264
As a crew
member, we want you to know

77
00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:42.300
that you're not
just part of a team,

78
00:10:42.302 --> 00:10:44.137
you're part of
our family.

79
00:10:48.508 --> 00:10:50.441
No, no, no.
That doesn't go through.

80
00:10:50.443 --> 00:10:51.910
Have
a complaint?

81
00:10:51.912 --> 00:10:54.314
Address it
to your superior officer.

82
00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.248
Oh, yes, working.

83
00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.618
I just got to find
the nearest pods.

84
00:11:04.023 --> 00:11:08.526
Senior engineers,
please report to engineering.

85
00:11:08.528 --> 00:11:09.596
Rodrigo, right?

86
00:11:11.631 --> 00:11:12.532
Yeah.

87
00:11:13.066 --> 00:11:14.100
Norah.

88
00:11:15.101 --> 00:11:16.334
I-I know.

89
00:11:16.336 --> 00:11:18.104
I usually work
with the day shift.

90
00:11:20.975 --> 00:11:23.608
- Can you...? Can you help me out here?
- Sure, I can.

91
00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:28.279
Um, are you a computer engineer
or something?

92
00:11:28.281 --> 00:11:29.982
- Mechanical.
- Okay.

93
00:11:29.984 --> 00:11:31.249
I can reset breakers.

94
00:11:31.251 --> 00:11:34.354
I've been down here for a bit.

95
00:11:43.162 --> 00:11:45.129
Hey, you gotta know...

96
00:11:45.131 --> 00:11:46.466
that wasn't our fault.

97
00:11:47.634 --> 00:11:49.667
I mean,
you-you saved the entire rig.

98
00:11:49.669 --> 00:11:51.602
I... I didn't even know
to close the door.

99
00:11:51.604 --> 00:11:52.505
Hmm.

100
00:11:58.678 --> 00:12:00.311
Bulkheads closed.

101
00:12:00.313 --> 00:12:03.548
Do you... Do you really think
that was an earthquake?

102
00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.384
No.

103
00:12:06.052 --> 00:12:07.453
I-I don't know.

104
00:12:10.089 --> 00:12:11.422
That's not good.

105
00:12:11.424 --> 00:12:13.624
The hardline's been severed.

106
00:12:13.626 --> 00:12:17.094
Antenna's gone. I don't even
think we can reach the surface.

107
00:12:17.096 --> 00:12:19.730
...to the nearest
escape pod as soon as possible.

108
00:12:19.732 --> 00:12:21.835
There's-there's
evac pods in CR-7.

109
00:12:29.977 --> 00:12:31.845
Hey, we got this, all right?

110
00:12:40.219 --> 00:12:42.522
Some of this water
is definitely sewage.

111
00:12:53.834 --> 00:12:56.034
Welcome
aboard the Kepler Station,

112
00:12:56.036 --> 00:12:58.937
located just a mile away
from the Roebuck...

113
00:12:58.939 --> 00:13:01.639
The titan-class
sister station...

114
00:13:01.641 --> 00:13:03.576
The Kepler...
pumps a crude...

115
00:13:05.879 --> 00:13:07.345
There we go.

116
00:13:07.347 --> 00:13:08.813
and we hope
you enjoy your stay.

117
00:13:08.815 --> 00:13:10.348
Can we...
Can we dig through there?

118
00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.149
I'll look inside.

119
00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.166
Yeah, I can fit up here,
if you can.

120
00:13:29.168 --> 00:13:30.236
Come check.

121
00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:36.041
Hello?

122
00:13:36.043 --> 00:13:37.310
Can anyone hear me?

123
00:13:38.645 --> 00:13:41.312
Hello? Hello?

124
00:13:41.314 --> 00:13:42.881
Hey, do you hear that?

125
00:13:42.883 --> 00:13:44.782
- Hey!
- Hello!

126
00:13:44.784 --> 00:13:46.452
Hey, keep talking, man.
I can hear you.

127
00:13:48.154 --> 00:13:49.522
I'm under the rock!

128
00:13:55.129 --> 00:13:56.460
Take him, take him.

129
00:13:56.462 --> 00:13:59.530
Paul? Here, here, here, here.
Hey, you.

130
00:13:59.532 --> 00:14:01.365
What's-what's going on
down there? Your legs all right?

131
00:14:01.367 --> 00:14:02.266
- Yeah.
- Okay.

132
00:14:02.268 --> 00:14:03.467
What do you need?

133
00:14:03.469 --> 00:14:04.769
To get the heck out of here.

134
00:14:04.771 --> 00:14:06.504
Yeah, yeah, I know.
What can I do?

135
00:14:06.506 --> 00:14:07.875
- All right, all right.
- All right.

136
00:14:10.576 --> 00:14:11.409
- You good?
- Yeah.

137
00:14:11.411 --> 00:14:13.611
All right.

138
00:14:13.613 --> 00:14:14.645
- All right. Here.
- Hey.

139
00:14:14.647 --> 00:14:17.015
- Norah?
- You're good. Hi!

140
00:14:17.017 --> 00:14:18.282
Yes.

141
00:14:18.284 --> 00:14:20.418
You sweet,
flat-chested elven creature.

142
00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.721
Okay, just breathe for a second.
You're all good.

143
00:14:23.723 --> 00:14:25.023
- Is Lil Paul okay?
- Yeah, he's cool.

144
00:14:25.025 --> 00:14:26.824
- Let me help you.
- You wanna try to stand up?

145
00:14:26.827 --> 00:14:29.161
- Yeah.
- All right, buddy. Here we go.

146
00:14:29.163 --> 00:14:30.394
Grab his arm?

147
00:14:30.396 --> 00:14:32.229
No, no, no. Wait. No, no.

148
00:14:32.231 --> 00:14:33.631
Okay, are you caught
in anything?

149
00:14:33.633 --> 00:14:35.967
No, no, no,
let's just be stronger.

150
00:14:40.074 --> 00:14:41.372
Okay.

151
00:14:41.374 --> 00:14:42.773
Okay, give me Lil Paul.

152
00:14:42.775 --> 00:14:43.909
- Yeah, here.
- Thank you.

153
00:14:43.911 --> 00:14:45.110
Gotta go.

154
00:14:45.112 --> 00:14:47.378
Okay, I got my robe
and my lucky sock.

155
00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.880
What are we doing?

156
00:14:48.882 --> 00:14:50.048
The evac pods in CR-7.

157
00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.850
- We're headed there, okay?
- Okay.

158
00:14:51.852 --> 00:14:54.119
The upper decks are collapsing.
We gotta move fast.

159
00:14:54.121 --> 00:14:55.286
Through that thing?

160
00:14:55.288 --> 00:14:57.388
You guys are crazy.

161
00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:58.691
I'm a big boy.

162
00:15:17.643 --> 00:15:19.777
All right. I think...

163
00:15:19.779 --> 00:15:20.713
Hold up.

164
00:15:36.596 --> 00:15:38.431
Bulkheads closed.

165
00:15:39.432 --> 00:15:41.233
Flooding contained.

166
00:15:41.235 --> 00:15:42.299
Okay.

167
00:15:51.811 --> 00:15:53.479
- You guys okay?
- Yeah.

168
00:15:58.551 --> 00:16:00.952
There's-there's someone up here.

169
00:16:00.954 --> 00:16:02.522
It's... It's McClellen.

170
00:16:31.852 --> 00:16:32.986
Jesus.

171
00:16:33.887 --> 00:16:34.922
Hey, Rod.

172
00:16:36.422 --> 00:16:37.557
Come on, bud.

173
00:16:50.137 --> 00:16:51.602
Guys, I see the pod bay.

174
00:16:51.604 --> 00:16:54.206
Attention! Attention!

175
00:16:54.208 --> 00:16:55.775
All Kepler crew...

176
00:16:56.844 --> 00:16:57.976
Cap?

177
00:16:57.978 --> 00:16:59.743
Holy shit.
He stayed behind?

178
00:17:01.414 --> 00:17:02.948
Wait, why's he
just sitting there?

179
00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.082
Oh, shit.

180
00:17:04.084 --> 00:17:06.184
"Shit?" What's...
What's "oh shit"? What?

181
00:17:06.186 --> 00:17:07.919
The evac pods are gone.

182
00:17:07.921 --> 00:17:09.689
- I need the line open.
- Captain!

183
00:17:13.827 --> 00:17:14.893
Hey!

184
00:17:14.895 --> 00:17:17.195
Norah. You're alive.

185
00:17:17.197 --> 00:17:18.296
Cap.

186
00:17:18.298 --> 00:17:19.498
The door's jammed.

187
00:17:22.002 --> 00:17:23.434
Rodrigo, Paul.

188
00:17:23.436 --> 00:17:25.736
I need you two to check where
we are on submersible. Now.

189
00:17:25.738 --> 00:17:28.173
All right, all right.

190
00:17:28.175 --> 00:17:31.109
On a scale from one to ten,
how bad's my rig?

191
00:17:34.147 --> 00:17:35.015
Uh, ten.

192
00:17:38.417 --> 00:17:40.218
You're 70% compromised.

193
00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.121
Honestly, you-you breathe
too hard in here, we're...

194
00:17:44.992 --> 00:17:46.523
Wait. Let me see.

195
00:17:46.525 --> 00:17:49.127
I don't get it. Was that
like an earthquake or...

196
00:17:49.129 --> 00:17:51.564
I don't know.
I'm trying to figure it out.

197
00:17:54.067 --> 00:17:55.532
Why are you still here?

198
00:17:55.534 --> 00:17:57.269
You should have gone up.
There were pods here.

199
00:17:57.271 --> 00:17:58.736
'Cause that's what captains do.

200
00:17:58.738 --> 00:18:01.174
Who cares? You have a kid,
you should have gone up.

201
00:18:03.676 --> 00:18:05.379
Can you, uh, can you
sit down, please?

202
00:18:07.347 --> 00:18:08.646
Any one of us would have
shoved your ass

203
00:18:08.648 --> 00:18:09.613
onto that pod immediately.

204
00:18:09.615 --> 00:18:10.849
Listen to me.

205
00:18:10.851 --> 00:18:12.317
Everybody's getting out
of here alive,

206
00:18:12.319 --> 00:18:13.484
you hear me?

207
00:18:13.486 --> 00:18:14.654
Okay?

208
00:18:16.223 --> 00:18:17.423
Hold that on your ear.

209
00:18:19.592 --> 00:18:21.425
I already sent 22 up.

210
00:18:21.427 --> 00:18:22.559
Smith reported seven dead.

211
00:18:22.561 --> 00:18:23.929
I found three.

212
00:18:23.931 --> 00:18:26.664
It was, it was Lee,
Travis and McClellen,

213
00:18:26.666 --> 00:18:28.465
and, um, um, McCl...

214
00:18:28.467 --> 00:18:29.834
McClellen's hands
were still warm

215
00:18:29.836 --> 00:18:31.702
so I-I know it was McClellen.

216
00:18:31.704 --> 00:18:33.637
I mean, she lives
three floors up,

217
00:18:33.639 --> 00:18:35.606
and I was brushing my teeth,
like, two hours ago.

218
00:18:35.608 --> 00:18:37.342
- I-I had to shut the door on the entire East wing.
- Don't do this to yourself.

219
00:18:37.344 --> 00:18:39.210
So, actually, you know what,
there could be more.

220
00:18:39.212 --> 00:18:40.511
Stop thinking back,
look forward.

221
00:18:40.513 --> 00:18:42.981
Look forward. Look at me.

222
00:18:42.983 --> 00:18:46.284
Now you follow the light.
Come on.

223
00:18:46.286 --> 00:18:47.888
Follow the light.
Ça va ça va.

224
00:18:49.689 --> 00:18:51.990
Cap,
that isa no-go on the submersibles.

225
00:18:51.992 --> 00:18:53.158
Copy that.

226
00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:55.095
I'm sending Norah
to the control room.

227
00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:02.133
Emily, are you okay? Hey.

228
00:19:02.135 --> 00:19:03.567
- Oh, my gosh. You're alive.
- Norah?

229
00:19:03.569 --> 00:19:04.804
- Hey.
- You're alive.

230
00:19:05.805 --> 00:19:07.339
- Dude.
- Ah, I hate that.

231
00:19:07.341 --> 00:19:09.174
- Have you heard anything?
- No, no. Nothing.

232
00:19:11.211 --> 00:19:13.011
- How are the cooling towers?
- I haven't checked 'em yet.

233
00:19:13.013 --> 00:19:14.079
- You wanna do it?
- Yeah, yeah.

234
00:19:14.081 --> 00:19:15.981
See if anybody's
alive out there.

235
00:19:15.983 --> 00:19:17.581
compromised.

236
00:19:17.583 --> 00:19:19.719
Bulkheads closed...

237
00:19:21.088 --> 00:19:22.488
Hey, hey.

238
00:19:26.226 --> 00:19:28.293
Someone's coming. Right?

239
00:19:28.295 --> 00:19:29.828
They're gonna...
They're gonna send someone.

240
00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.296
I don't know. Thank you.

241
00:19:31.298 --> 00:19:33.064
I'm pretty sure
they already sent someone.

242
00:19:33.066 --> 00:19:36.101
I'm less sure we have the time
to wait for them.

243
00:19:36.103 --> 00:19:37.202
- Norah.
- Yeah.

244
00:19:37.204 --> 00:19:40.671
So, the cooling towers?
What are we getting?

245
00:19:42.075 --> 00:19:43.074
Oh, um...

246
00:19:44.277 --> 00:19:45.910
Nothing good.

247
00:19:45.912 --> 00:19:47.544
All the upper decks
have collapsed

248
00:19:47.546 --> 00:19:49.813
and we lost the cooling towers.

249
00:19:49.815 --> 00:19:51.850
The core of the Kepler
is completely unstable.

250
00:19:51.852 --> 00:19:53.084
Wait, what do you
mean "unstable"?

251
00:19:53.086 --> 00:19:54.551
Like, poof,
we all die "unstable"?

252
00:19:54.553 --> 00:19:55.519
What are we
talking about here, Norah?

253
00:19:55.521 --> 00:19:57.355
The thermal cores.

254
00:19:57.357 --> 00:19:59.190
That's a lot of energy
with nowhere to go.

255
00:19:59.192 --> 00:20:00.992
Okay, the intern's
freaking me out.

256
00:20:00.994 --> 00:20:02.726
Can somebody just explain
what the hell's going on here?

257
00:20:02.728 --> 00:20:04.062
Research assistant.

258
00:20:04.064 --> 00:20:05.763
No, there-there... There's a...
There's a, um...

259
00:20:05.765 --> 00:20:06.998
If there's a meltdown,
there's gonna be a lot of heat.

260
00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.766
There's gonna be
a flash boil, explosions.

261
00:20:08.768 --> 00:20:10.869
I don't really know. I watch a
lot of anime. That's all I know.

262
00:20:10.871 --> 00:20:12.437
Oh, you watch anime?
I like anime.

263
00:20:15.442 --> 00:20:16.807
No, I mean, he's right.

264
00:20:16.809 --> 00:20:18.943
We have about 30 minutes
till meltdown.

265
00:20:18.945 --> 00:20:21.880
And, uh, it's gonna blow us
into tiny pieces to the surface.

266
00:20:21.882 --> 00:20:24.115
And people are gonna find us,
like, floating around.

267
00:20:24.117 --> 00:20:26.518
Bulkhead compromised.

268
00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.253
Okay, guys, listen.

269
00:20:28.255 --> 00:20:31.423
The escape pods are gone
and the sub is out of order.

270
00:20:31.425 --> 00:20:33.791
And we're not getting
any more radio signals.

271
00:20:33.793 --> 00:20:35.894
And the structure of the Kepler
is totally unsound.

272
00:20:35.896 --> 00:20:37.694
Captain, there better be
a good punchline,

273
00:20:37.696 --> 00:20:38.762
'cause this setup is...

274
00:20:38.764 --> 00:20:40.133
- So weak.
- weak.

275
00:20:42.768 --> 00:20:44.436
We go for the Roebuck.

276
00:20:44.438 --> 00:20:46.271
The Roebuck?

277
00:20:46.273 --> 00:20:47.972
It's a mile down
and a mile that way.

278
00:20:47.974 --> 00:20:49.541
- What are you talking about?
- Yeah.

279
00:20:49.543 --> 00:20:51.044
How would we even get there?

280
00:20:53.313 --> 00:20:54.379
We walk.

281
00:20:54.381 --> 00:20:55.447
We what?

282
00:20:55.449 --> 00:20:56.481
Walk.

283
00:20:56.483 --> 00:20:58.083
We walk?

284
00:20:58.085 --> 00:21:00.218
That's what you dug me
out of the rubble for?

285
00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.286
I can't walk.

286
00:21:01.288 --> 00:21:02.420
I don't even have a suit.

287
00:21:02.422 --> 00:21:04.556
Listen, listen. Listen to me.

288
00:21:04.558 --> 00:21:07.225
Here's what we're gonna do.

289
00:21:07.227 --> 00:21:10.328
We're gonna drop down to the
cargo elevator to the seafloor.

290
00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:14.099
Then we use the access tunnel
to get to the Midpoint station.

291
00:21:14.101 --> 00:21:17.068
There we can charge
and clean the rebreathers.

292
00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.237
And then we follow the markers

293
00:21:19.239 --> 00:21:22.173
across the plateau
to the Roebuck.

294
00:21:24.945 --> 00:21:26.544
So we just go in the pitch black

295
00:21:26.546 --> 00:21:28.346
and we walk without knowing
where we're going

296
00:21:28.348 --> 00:21:29.613
with insufficient oxygen?

297
00:21:29.615 --> 00:21:31.082
- That's the plan?
- That's the plan.

298
00:21:31.084 --> 00:21:32.616
Everybody down with that?
Norah, you okay with that?

299
00:21:32.618 --> 00:21:34.853
The suits can't be down there
that long. You know that.

300
00:21:34.855 --> 00:21:37.355
Not everyone here
is an experienced diver and...

301
00:21:37.357 --> 00:21:38.456
Than we never know.

302
00:21:38.458 --> 00:21:39.926
I'm-I'm not trying to be...

303
00:21:41.194 --> 00:21:43.161
Can you just admit
we might die doing that?

304
00:21:43.163 --> 00:21:46.665
Yeah. But can you admit
that we might live doing this?

305
00:21:47.868 --> 00:21:49.300
Hey, what about
the old Shepard Station?

306
00:21:49.302 --> 00:21:50.602
Isn't that closer?

307
00:21:50.604 --> 00:21:53.404
Shepard Station's gone.
There's nothing there.

308
00:21:53.406 --> 00:21:56.376
Uh, you guys,
you need to hear this.

309
00:21:58.845 --> 00:22:00.245
Can this be
something good?

310
00:22:00.247 --> 00:22:02.213
Could we please have
one good thing? Could we?

311
00:22:02.215 --> 00:22:04.748
I think this was the last
transmission from the drill site.

312
00:22:07.653 --> 00:22:09.820
Mayday, mayday!

313
00:22:09.822 --> 00:22:12.290
We've been compromised by category ten...

314
00:22:23.702 --> 00:22:25.203
Now, what the hell
was that noise?

315
00:22:28.441 --> 00:22:30.942
Also, the temperature outside
jumped ten degrees.

316
00:22:30.944 --> 00:22:33.945
Great, so it'll be warm when
we're walking across the plateau.

317
00:22:33.947 --> 00:22:35.880
The water doesn't do that.
That's impossible.

318
00:22:38.151 --> 00:22:41.152
That's just aftershocks
from the last earthquake, okay?

319
00:22:41.154 --> 00:22:43.021
It's 'cause
we drilled too deep. Okay?

320
00:22:43.023 --> 00:22:44.923
It's those tectonic plates
I talk about all the time.

321
00:22:44.925 --> 00:22:47.724
This is insane.
Okay, this is insane.

322
00:22:47.726 --> 00:22:49.162
We go for the Roebuck.

323
00:22:59.472 --> 00:23:01.372
What? If we're gonna
do this, let's do it!

324
00:23:01.374 --> 00:23:02.309
Am I right?

325
00:23:05.011 --> 00:23:06.710
All right, we can compromise.
I can turn it down.

326
00:23:08.281 --> 00:23:09.514
Emily.

327
00:23:09.516 --> 00:23:11.418
Lose your pants.
They won't fit in the suit.

328
00:23:14.187 --> 00:23:16.089
Deck A compromised.

329
00:23:18.491 --> 00:23:20.458
Bulkheads closed.

330
00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:21.995
Flooding contained.

331
00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:38.044
Has anyone ever
walked out there before?

332
00:23:40.247 --> 00:23:42.249
Longer than to fix a pipe.
I mean, just...

333
00:23:43.816 --> 00:23:44.951
Just walked?

334
00:23:46.253 --> 00:23:47.087
No.

335
00:23:49.122 --> 00:23:50.787
Check if we have enough helmets.

336
00:23:50.789 --> 00:23:52.791
I just need you to find
six good ones.

337
00:23:58.131 --> 00:23:59.232
Hey, Norah.

338
00:23:59.798 --> 00:24:01.332
Hey.

339
00:24:01.334 --> 00:24:02.936
- Thank you.
- Yeah, sure.

340
00:24:04.971 --> 00:24:07.007
Hey. How you doing?

341
00:24:07.607 --> 00:24:08.840
You ready?

342
00:24:08.842 --> 00:24:09.943
All right.

343
00:24:19.286 --> 00:24:21.087
These are ripped too? Come on!

344
00:24:30.830 --> 00:24:31.998
All right, this is gonna suck.

345
00:24:32.732 --> 00:24:34.165
Okay.

346
00:24:34.167 --> 00:24:35.967
Oh, sorry, sorry!

347
00:24:35.969 --> 00:24:38.336
Okay. Good?

348
00:24:38.338 --> 00:24:39.306
Go suit up.

349
00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:46.012
Your air is good.

350
00:24:56.356 --> 00:24:57.655
Thank you.

351
00:24:57.657 --> 00:24:59.859
Okay, clear
all this shit from the deck.

352
00:25:10.637 --> 00:25:12.170
What are you thinking?

353
00:25:12.172 --> 00:25:13.137
I'm thinking
I really didn't like

354
00:25:13.139 --> 00:25:15.573
the sound on that transmission.

355
00:25:15.575 --> 00:25:16.609
We should take something.

356
00:25:19.312 --> 00:25:20.246
Yeah.

357
00:25:21.047 --> 00:25:23.114
That's a very valid point.

358
00:25:23.116 --> 00:25:25.950
Okay. Let me see your back.

359
00:25:25.952 --> 00:25:27.454
Okay. Last checks.

360
00:25:29.389 --> 00:25:30.223
Let's go.

361
00:25:32.792 --> 00:25:34.792
All right, listen up.

362
00:25:34.794 --> 00:25:38.396
We watch our descent rate
and follow all safety protocols.

363
00:25:38.398 --> 00:25:40.934
Remember,
these suits are dangerous.

364
00:25:44.371 --> 00:25:45.972
Hey, what's so funny?

365
00:25:50.076 --> 00:25:52.710
- I can't do this. I can't.
- Yes, you can.

366
00:25:52.712 --> 00:25:55.179
Yes, you can. Yes, you can.
Yes, you can.

367
00:25:55.181 --> 00:25:57.949
It's all right. It's all right.
It's just an elevator, all right?

368
00:25:57.951 --> 00:25:59.751
It's all lit up
to the weigh station.

369
00:25:59.753 --> 00:26:00.752
You just follow the pipeline.

370
00:26:00.754 --> 00:26:03.521
You can do it. Come on, come on.

371
00:26:03.523 --> 00:26:05.525
Hey, what's the scariest
part of a roller coaster?

372
00:26:06.593 --> 00:26:08.326
Waiting in line.

373
00:26:09.763 --> 00:26:10.630
Ready?

374
00:26:12.332 --> 00:26:14.766
I'm gonna be right there
with you. Every step.

375
00:26:14.768 --> 00:26:16.734
Main bridge compromised.

376
00:26:16.736 --> 00:26:17.904
We have to move.

377
00:26:19.072 --> 00:26:20.972
All right.
Everybody in the pool.

378
00:26:20.974 --> 00:26:22.273
Okay, we gotta go.

379
00:26:22.275 --> 00:26:24.308
That was one level above us.

380
00:26:24.310 --> 00:26:26.110
This one's next. Let's go.

381
00:26:26.112 --> 00:26:27.914
integrity compromised.

382
00:26:29.249 --> 00:26:32.750
Structural integrity
compromised.

383
00:26:32.752 --> 00:26:33.684
Take us down.

384
00:26:33.686 --> 00:26:35.420
"If you don't know
where you're going,

385
00:26:35.422 --> 00:26:37.722
any road can get
you there."

386
00:26:37.724 --> 00:26:38.891
Dude.

387
00:26:38.893 --> 00:26:40.525
What? It's not me, Norah.
It's from a book.

388
00:26:40.527 --> 00:26:41.492
Let's go.

389
00:26:42.996 --> 00:26:44.264
We all know you
can't read.

390
00:27:12.592 --> 00:27:14.292
All right,
I don't wanna scare anyone,

391
00:27:14.294 --> 00:27:15.660
but once we get
to the depth

392
00:27:15.662 --> 00:27:17.630
we're gonna have to
jump to the cargo lift.

393
00:27:22.001 --> 00:27:24.402
Okay, here we go.
Shit.

394
00:27:24.404 --> 00:27:27.004
Exterior hatch,
it's ripped to shreds.

395
00:27:27.006 --> 00:27:28.105
Everybody, get ready.

396
00:27:28.107 --> 00:27:29.240
Hang onto
something 'cause

397
00:27:29.242 --> 00:27:31.242
pressure's gonna
hit us hard.

398
00:27:31.244 --> 00:27:32.343
Override it.

399
00:27:32.345 --> 00:27:33.980
As long as it opens,
we'll be fine.

400
00:27:35.748 --> 00:27:38.015
Captain, I don't know
what's going on with this thing.

401
00:27:38.017 --> 00:27:38.917
Well,
keep trying.

402
00:27:41.988 --> 00:27:42.955
Rodrigo.

403
00:27:42.957 --> 00:27:44.255
Guys, what's going on?

404
00:27:44.257 --> 00:27:46.125
Keep the door closed.
Keep the door closed!

405
00:27:58.171 --> 00:28:00.607
Stay where you are.
Close your eyes.

406
00:28:02.342 --> 00:28:04.744
It's okay, Em.
You're good, you're good.

407
00:28:07.180 --> 00:28:08.881
Listen. Listen.

408
00:28:08.883 --> 00:28:10.781
Close your eyes.

409
00:28:47.955 --> 00:28:50.454
Let's go, Emily.
Step to the edge.

410
00:28:50.456 --> 00:28:51.658
You have to jump now.

411
00:28:54.060 --> 00:28:56.095
Norah, he's gone.

412
00:28:57.497 --> 00:28:59.165
It's your turn.
You need to jump.

413
00:29:17.350 --> 00:29:19.550
He knew that
that helmet was faulty.

414
00:29:19.552 --> 00:29:21.154
I mean, I-I-I know
that he knew it.

415
00:29:21.588 --> 00:29:22.820
Listen.

416
00:29:22.822 --> 00:29:25.456
I know how you feel.
I know it's unfair.

417
00:29:27.760 --> 00:29:30.028
But you're gonna have to
take it and use it.

418
00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:31.698
Yeah. Okay.

419
00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:33.764
Come on.

420
00:29:33.766 --> 00:29:34.565
The sooner we get clear

421
00:29:34.567 --> 00:29:35.702
of the station the better.

422
00:30:02.128 --> 00:30:04.163
I've never seen
anyone die before.

423
00:30:07.433 --> 00:30:09.268
I saw somebody die.

424
00:30:11.537 --> 00:30:13.506
I've never seen anybody implode.

425
00:30:21.115 --> 00:30:22.747
What are you laughing at?

426
00:30:22.749 --> 00:30:24.116
Uh, I was just
thinking of this thing

427
00:30:24.118 --> 00:30:26.217
that Rodrigo did sometimes.

428
00:30:26.219 --> 00:30:27.551
He'd always say
he had a new joke,

429
00:30:27.553 --> 00:30:29.520
and then he'd tell
the same stupid joke.

430
00:30:29.522 --> 00:30:32.860
I was... laughing at that joke.

431
00:30:34.128 --> 00:30:35.760
Yeah, what was it?

432
00:30:35.762 --> 00:30:38.729
What did the fish say when
it bumped into the brick wall?

433
00:30:42.168 --> 00:30:43.236
"Dam."

434
00:30:45.039 --> 00:30:46.872
Pretty stupid joke.

435
00:31:08.728 --> 00:31:10.227
It looks like
whatever it is

436
00:31:10.229 --> 00:31:11.830
might be on the deck below us.

437
00:31:13.901 --> 00:31:17.135
I think it's a distress signal
from one of the pods.

438
00:31:17.137 --> 00:31:18.371
How far?

439
00:31:19.205 --> 00:31:20.972
Two hundred more meters.

440
00:31:20.974 --> 00:31:23.274
Why wouldn't it be
going to the surface?

441
00:31:23.276 --> 00:31:24.677
Maybe it's only got
half a charge.

442
00:31:25.979 --> 00:31:27.445
Uh...

443
00:31:27.447 --> 00:31:29.248
It's definitely stopped
on the platform below us.

444
00:31:29.950 --> 00:31:30.851
Survivor.

445
00:31:31.551 --> 00:31:32.920
It could be a survivor.

446
00:31:34.821 --> 00:31:37.621
Guys, somebody's gonna
have to suit up.

447
00:31:37.623 --> 00:31:39.590
All right, Emily,
this is your time.

448
00:31:39.592 --> 00:31:40.560
What?

449
00:31:41.427 --> 00:31:42.562
I'm just messing with you.

450
00:31:44.430 --> 00:31:46.532
Here, take him.

451
00:31:48.267 --> 00:31:49.868
Take this bunny.

452
00:31:49.870 --> 00:31:50.904
I bequeath it to you.

453
00:31:51.972 --> 00:31:54.139
If he doesn't make it,
I'll haunt you.

454
00:31:54.141 --> 00:31:55.573
Let's go, guys.

455
00:31:55.575 --> 00:31:57.843
We don't know how long
until the Kepler blows.

456
00:31:57.845 --> 00:31:59.777
Let's go put
our lives in danger.

457
00:31:59.779 --> 00:32:01.614
- Be careful.
- We'll be right back.

458
00:32:04.484 --> 00:32:07.152
Paul's crazy. Right?

459
00:32:07.154 --> 00:32:10.188
Yeah. I guess so.

460
00:32:10.190 --> 00:32:12.389
Hey,
Captain, what do we do?

461
00:32:12.391 --> 00:32:13.992
With the body, when we find it.

462
00:32:13.994 --> 00:32:16.128
We're talking about
a possible survivor, Paul.

463
00:32:16.130 --> 00:32:17.328
Okay.

464
00:32:17.330 --> 00:32:19.064
Then hypothetically.

465
00:32:19.066 --> 00:32:21.799
Let's say we were to come
across a body and it was dead.

466
00:32:21.801 --> 00:32:24.936
Just grab something
we can take back to his family.

467
00:32:24.938 --> 00:32:26.506
It's okay. I
know what to do.

468
00:32:28.441 --> 00:32:30.708
Oh, really?
We got G.I. Joe over here.

469
00:32:30.710 --> 00:32:33.344
And we are about to touch...

470
00:32:33.346 --> 00:32:38.216
in three, two, one.

471
00:32:42.055 --> 00:32:43.054
We're locked in.

472
00:32:43.056 --> 00:32:44.055
All right.

473
00:32:44.057 --> 00:32:45.058
- Ready?
- Yeah.

474
00:32:46.592 --> 00:32:48.559
Yeah. Yeah!

475
00:32:48.561 --> 00:32:50.228
Let's get this done
before the Kepler

476
00:32:50.230 --> 00:32:51.462
comes down on our asses.

477
00:32:51.464 --> 00:32:52.998
Okay.

478
00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:56.801
Turn on all the camera feeds
we have available.

479
00:32:56.803 --> 00:32:58.970
How long can
someone survive in a pod?

480
00:32:58.972 --> 00:33:00.874
If he lost power, not long.

481
00:33:02.242 --> 00:33:03.743
Especially at this depth.

482
00:33:05.511 --> 00:33:08.046
Okay, guys, we're starting
the decompression now.

483
00:33:08.048 --> 00:33:10.349
Are either of you two married?

484
00:33:13.053 --> 00:33:14.485
Was.

485
00:33:14.487 --> 00:33:15.488
Kids?

486
00:33:16.190 --> 00:33:17.255
Daughter.

487
00:33:17.257 --> 00:33:18.322
How-how old is she?

488
00:33:18.324 --> 00:33:19.925
Fourteen.

489
00:33:19.927 --> 00:33:21.592
That's a tough age for a girl.

490
00:33:21.594 --> 00:33:23.931
I mean, it's-it's a phase.
It will pass.

491
00:33:24.564 --> 00:33:26.131
She's not 14.

492
00:33:26.133 --> 00:33:28.399
Allie? She's gotta be
like my age, right?

493
00:33:28.401 --> 00:33:30.369
Who said 14? Did I say that?

494
00:33:31.171 --> 00:33:32.403
Yeah.

495
00:33:32.405 --> 00:33:34.405
Well, I don't know
why I said it.

496
00:33:34.407 --> 00:33:35.606
You're losing it, old man.

497
00:33:35.608 --> 00:33:37.142
You're going senile down here.

498
00:33:37.144 --> 00:33:40.744
It's actually a normal
neurological reaction.

499
00:33:40.746 --> 00:33:41.847
When you're facing death,
time just...

500
00:33:41.849 --> 00:33:42.983
Listen to me. Listen to me.

501
00:33:44.817 --> 00:33:47.054
You're not gonna die. Okay?

502
00:33:50.456 --> 00:33:51.524
All right.

503
00:33:52.192 --> 00:33:54.159
Worst idea ever.

504
00:33:54.161 --> 00:33:56.560
Let's do it anyway.

505
00:33:56.562 --> 00:33:58.362
Helmets on.
Locked and loaded.

506
00:33:58.364 --> 00:33:59.630
Either of you have dogs?

507
00:33:59.632 --> 00:34:00.731
Flood it, Norah!

508
00:34:00.733 --> 00:34:02.733
Flooding.

509
00:34:04.905 --> 00:34:05.839
I have a corgi.

510
00:34:07.875 --> 00:34:11.977
Not house-trained, so he's
kind of a nightmare right now,

511
00:34:11.979 --> 00:34:13.811
but I didn't think
I would miss him this much.

512
00:34:13.813 --> 00:34:16.749
Okay, hatch is sealed.
We're outside.

513
00:34:18.684 --> 00:34:20.020
Okay, I'll put us on standby.

514
00:34:21.121 --> 00:34:22.455
Turn the floodlights on, please.

515
00:34:33.033 --> 00:34:35.901
Cap, this platform's
not too stable.

516
00:34:35.903 --> 00:34:38.071
I, uh, don't know how long
we should be out here.

517
00:34:51.118 --> 00:34:52.752
Oh, God.

518
00:34:57.523 --> 00:35:00.125
Guys, keep on walking forward.

519
00:35:00.127 --> 00:35:01.359
Like 20 meters.

520
00:35:01.361 --> 00:35:02.762
Check what's
on the right.

521
00:35:06.300 --> 00:35:09.167
I can't see shit.
My right or his right?

522
00:35:14.774 --> 00:35:15.608
What the
hell is that?

523
00:35:19.846 --> 00:35:21.478
